# Content writing standards

## Voice

Sound: confident, intelligent, modern, direct, experienced, commercially sophisticated, performance-driven, transparent, human. American English.

Do not sound: spammy, flashy, desperate, overly corporate, overly technical, like an affiliate scheme, call center, or generic AI copy.

## Copy principles

CLEAR > CLEVER · SPECIFIC > GENERIC · CREDIBLE > IMPRESSIVE · OUTCOMES > FEATURES · CONVERSATIONS > CLICKS · QUALITY > VOLUME

Lead with outcomes. Short active sentences. Sophistication comes from business understanding, not jargon.

## Value props (use naturally — do not spam the slogan)

Primary: “Turning digital demand into qualified customer conversations.”  
Supports: performance-driven acquisition, in-house media buying, qualified inbound calls, Pay Per Call expertise, campaign optimization, measurable performance, scalable acquisition, media/publisher relationships.

Preferred terms: qualified inbound calls, high-intent consumer inquiries, customer conversations, inbound customer opportunities.

## CTAs

**Buyer:** Discuss a Campaign · Start a Conversation · Talk to Our Team · Explore Our Solutions · Scale Your Customer Acquisition  

**Publisher:** Become a Media Partner · Partner With RidgeRise · Explore Campaign Opportunities  

**Avoid:** BUY CALLS NOW · BUY LEADS · GET CHEAP LEADS · GUARANTEED CUSTOMERS · GET CALLS TODAY

Feel like a strategic acquisition partner, not a commodity marketplace.

## Language to avoid

Cutting-edge / revolutionary / unlock unprecedented growth / supercharge / transform your digital presence / game-changing / next-generation / unparalleled / guaranteed growth / skyrocket  

Also avoid: “In today’s fast-paced digital landscape…,” “In today’s competitive marketplace…,” “Businesses today need…,” “Whether you’re a small business or large enterprise…”

```text
❌ Unlock synergistic omnichannel lead gen synergies at scale!!!
✅ We generate consumer demand through in-house media buying and connect high-intent callers with businesses ready to serve them.
```

## Homepage direction

Target advertisers first. Answer fast: what RidgeRise does (customer acquisition via performance marketing), how (in-house media buying, demand generation, Pay Per Call, partnerships), difference (internally generated demand + network scale), next step (Discuss a Campaign). Do not overwhelm with technical Pay Per Call jargon.

## Buyer journey (when explaining process)

1. Define the customer → 2. Build acquisition strategy → 3. Generate demand → 4. Connect intent → 5. Measure performance → 6. Optimize & scale  

Do not imply every campaign follows an identical workflow.

## Final quality test

If swapping “RidgeRise Media” for any random agency still works, rewrite — content is too generic. Visitor must know what RidgeRise does, trust the specificity, and know the next step.
